# LICENSE — Built-in Ambient Sound Set

All 89 sound files in this folder originate from the open-source
[Moodist](https://github.com/remvze/moodist) project (commit `main`,
tree `11c0be2`), where they live under `public/sounds/`.

## License status

Moodist's code is MIT (© 2023 MAE), but its README's "Third-Party
Assets" section explicitly excludes the sound files from that license
and states they are subject to either:

- the **Pixabay Content License** — https://pixabay.com/service/license-summary/
- or **CC0 1.0** (Creative Commons Zero)

The upstream project does **not** publish a per-file license mapping,
so an individual file's exact license between those two cannot be
verified from the repository. Both licenses grant free use,
modification, and distribution; neither requires attribution. The most
restrictive reading (Pixabay Content License) permits modification and
bundling into an application (as here) and only bars redistributing the
files as a standalone pack with no added creative value.

## Storage form

- WAV sources are stored as **FLAC** (lossless, level 8): each file
  decodes bit-exact to its upstream WAV (verified via PCM md5).
- MP3 sources are re-encoded to **Opus VBR at the transparency tier**
  (160 kbps stereo / 112 kbps mono — beyond the commonly cited
  transparency thresholds for each channel layout, with headroom for
  the lossy-to-lossy generation). Every output decodes cleanly and
  preserves the source duration.

